  "title": "For Your Pleasure",
  "country": "UK",
  "released": "1973-03-23",
  "notes": "Original UK release in fully laminated gatefold cover on 'pink rim/palm tree' labels.\nInside gatefold still has Island \"i\" logo with text below: \"island records ltd, basing street london wII\".\n• Later editions omit this address, as the move to St Peters Square was expected.\nSome copies include a poly-lined turquoise company inner sleeve with \"i\" logo and \"island records ltd basing street london w11\" in pink.\n\nRecorded at AIR Studios, London, February 1973\n\n℗ 1973 Island Records Ltd [labels]\n℗ 1973 Island Records [cover]\n\nPublished by E.G. Music Ltd. © 1973 [labels]\nAll songs published by E.G. Music Ltd © 1973 [cover]\n\n\"For Your Pleasure...\" subtitled \"The Second Roxy Music Album\" inside gatefold and on labels.\n\n• Produced by Chris Thomas and Roxy Music for E. G. Records, Special thanks to John Anthony [inside gatefold] but:\n• Produced by Chris Thomas and Roxy Music for E. G. Records Ltd. [label side A] and\n• Produced by John Anthony and Roxy Music for E. G. Records Ltd. [label side B].\n\nRunouts are stamped.\n",
  "released_formatted": "23 Mar 1973",
